    "updated_at": "2026-09-18T13:48:31Z",
    "body": "Another datapoint, on **2.1.276** (linux, cli entrypoint): still no switch, and the share gets worse as subagent context grows.\n\n**Measured** on one 1h45 interactive session driving four custom subagents (one long \"generator\" agent whose context reached ~380k on `claude-opus-5[1m]`), raw request/response bodies captured:\n\n| query_source | calls | cache read | cache write | uncached in | output |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| real agent + main-thread turns | 442 | 61.2 M | 1.53 M | 0.9 k | 328 k |\n| **`agent_summary`** | **103** | **21.8 M** | 4.9 k | 157.5 k | **2.1 k** |\n\nThat is **26 % of the session's cache-read tokens** for ~20 output tokens per call, one call every 30.8–31.3 s while an agent runs. Because the summary is a fork of the *whole* transcript on the *same* model, the cost per tick is the agent's current context size: a 380k-context agent pays ~45 M cache-read tokens per hour just for its spinner line.\n\n**Gating, as read in the 2.1.276 bundle** (for whoever plumbs the flag): the Agent tool launches the summarizer with\n\n```js\nenableSummarization: W_e() || (Pt || Dt) && !Te()\n// W_e = launchOptions.sdkAgentProgressSummariesEnabled()   (SDK option only)\n// Pt  = coordinator mode\n// Dt  = fork-subagent gate open && caller is not an in-process teammate\n// Te  = !launchOptions.isInteractive()\n```\n\nSo today the only levers are the ones already found in this thread: `CLAUDE_CODE_FORK_SUBAGENT=false` (which also drops `subagent_type: \"fork\"` and the forced-async launch that shares the `Dt` gate), or running non-interactively (`-p`), where it is off. `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_NARRATION` is indeed gone. The 30 s constant is still `intervalMs ?? 30000` with no caller passing `intervalMs`.\n\n+1 to a dedicated setting; failing that, an interval that scales with context size (or a tail-only fork) would remove most of the cost without losing the spinner.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
